  "review_conclusions": [
    "ResourceLocator parse first separates the scheme,then the first label delimiter,before field construction; new normalizes paths before rejecting an explicit empty label. The six added variant docs match static return paths without claiming an error-priority guarantee for multiple invalid fields.",
    "Non-package paths and the package's inner path use the same host Path component folding. Package ID admission and inner-root admission remain separate. These checks do not establish physical containment,file existence or package registration.",
    "AssetReference preserves an owned UUID/locator pair and the url wire field. Its readable and binary Serde branches use different field representations; neither checks registry pairing or replaces an existing asset UUID with a location-derived identity.",
    "Stable UUID framing fixes the version,namespace,component count and each byte length; the shared hash result receives version8/RFC bits. Asset UUID,resource label and asset-UUID-derived resource ID use separate domains. Memory resource IDs remain randomly allocated.",
    "Typed/untyped handles carry identity and kind information without a payload lease. Runtime get/snapshot/acquire separately check registry kind and concrete Arc payload type; the acquisition path owns residency release identity.",
    "Record builders only assemble candidates. Runtime commit owns revision,state transitions,payload changes and event projection; ordinary Error-to-Ready is rejected unless the operation carries recovery authorization. Error diagnostics alone do not change state, and last valid payload can remain readable after a failed reload.",
    "ResourceEvent is the net record projection,with removed-record revision and old locator on rename; event-log order and gaps are separate from resource revision.",
    "All eight owned tests were inspected for their actual assertions. JSON roundtrip,sample malformed package addresses,fixed UUID vector and display comparisons provide narrower evidence than binary Serde,allocation measurement,multiplatform execution or Runtime integration. The adjacent include_str guard selects only zr_resource internal sources."
  ],
